# The walk follows a hop past the target and treats reaching or passing the
# target as success, so a read returns a body no chain of hops produces.
MODULE: UpcastOrExplicitFailureOvershootAccepted
TARGET: UpcastOrExplicitFailure
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the upcaster walk accepts a hop that overshoots the target

--- FIND
    IF c = t THEN TRUE
    ELSE IF c > t \/ n = 0 THEN FALSE
    ELSE IF \E h \in EffH : h[1] = c /\ h[2] <= t
         THEN Walk((CHOOSE h \in EffH : h[1] = c /\ h[2] <= t)[2], t, n - 1)
--- REPLACE
    IF c >= t THEN TRUE
    ELSE IF n = 0 THEN FALSE
    ELSE IF \E h \in EffH : h[1] = c
         THEN Walk((CHOOSE h \in EffH : h[1] = c)[2], t, n - 1)
--- END